  "content": {
    "id": "p57-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Find the coordinates of point $Q$ where the tangent to the curve $y=5x^2-3x$ is parallel to the line $7x-y+3=0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$Q=(1,2)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}7x-y+3&=0\\\\y&=7x+3\\end{align*}$$\nThe line has gradient $7$, so the parallel tangent also has gradient $7$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=10x-3\\\\10x-3&=7\\\\x&=1\\\\y&=5(1)^2-3(1)\\\\y&=2\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $Q=(1,2)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
